WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.500
Mistral.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.769
A lab that treated efficiency as a product feature.

3
00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:06.167
Two tricks made it work.

4
00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.533
Trick one is sliding-window attention.

5
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:15.139
Each token attends only to the last w tokens, instead of everything before it.

6
00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:18.200
Mistral's window is four thousand ninety six.

7
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.600
Only a diagonal band of the causal matrix is computed, so cost drops toward n times w.

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.367
But does the model lose long-range context?

9
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:28.858
No.

10
00:00:28.858 --> 00:00:33.133
Layer two sees layer one's outputs, so information travels further.

11
00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.893
The reach grows by one window per layer.

12
00:00:35.893 --> 00:00:37.000
Depth restores it.

13
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.267
Trick two is grouped-query attention.

14
00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:46.600
Thirty two query heads share just eight key and value heads, shrinking the KV cache about four times.

15
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.633
Mixtral brought mixture-of-experts to open weights.

16
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:53.100
Each layer has eight expert networks.

17
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.767
A router activates only two per token.

18
00:00:56.067 --> 00:01:00.233
So you get large-model quality at a fraction of the per-token compute.

19
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:03.400
Both tricks are visible in the config.

20
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.567
We load it, then print the window, query heads, and key value heads.

21
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:11.867
Window four thousand ninety six, thirty two query heads sharing eight.

22
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.233
Here is the payoff.

23
00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:18.633
Your Q and A service runs on a single twenty-four gigabyte card.

24
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:24.200
With standard attention, twenty concurrent four thousand token sessions overflow memory.

25
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.076
With GQA the cache is a quarter the size.

26
00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:31.033
So the number of key value heads is a capacity-planning number.

27
00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.041
Let's recap.

28
00:01:33.041 --> 00:01:35.533
A sliding window cuts attention cost.

29
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:38.800
GQA shrinks the KV cache about four times.

30
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.367
Mixtral activates two of eight experts.

31
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.171
Efficiency is a product feature.

32
00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:45.267
Next up: Qwen.
